================================================================================
PART 1. Is the merge the identity it claims, and how big is the BCH gap?
================================================================================
     alpha    beta  |merge-target|  |orig-target|  |merge-orig|
  -------------------------------------------------------------
      0.10    0.10        6.10e-17       3.53e-03      3.53e-03
      0.50    0.30        1.24e-16       5.25e-02      5.25e-02
      1.50    0.90        2.37e-16       4.38e-01      4.38e-01
      3.80    0.94        3.72e-16       8.13e-01      8.13e-01
  col1 ~0 confirms the identity. col2/col3 are the real approximation gap:
  the merge equals exp(-i(aZ+bX)/2) exactly, and THAT differs from the
  original CRZ-then-CRX product by O(alpha*beta).

